      "agent_input": "Please read docs/q3_report.md and data/sales_q3.csv, then compare the Q3 new contract value in the report to the total won deals for James Okafor and Sofia Delgado. Let me know if the report needs to be updated.",
      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here are the results of my comparison:\n\n---\n\n## Report vs. CSV Comparison\n\n**Report (`q3_report.md`) states:**\n- Q3 New Contract Value: **$1,040,000** (across 14 closed deals)\n\n**CSV (`sales_q3.csv`) \u2014 Won deals for the two reps you asked about:**\n\n| Rep | Won Deals | Total |\n|---|---|---|\n| **James Okafor** | 7 deals | **$571,500** |\n| **Sofia Delgado** | 6 deals | **$460,000** |\n| **Combined (Okafor + Delgado)** | **13 deals** | **$1,031,500** |\n\n**The remaining won deal in the CSV:**\n- Marcus Webb (D014): **$8,500**\n\n**Total of ALL won deals in the CSV:** $1,031,500 + $8,500 = **$1,040,000** \u2705\n\n---\n\n## Verdict: The report's $1,040,000 new contract value is correct.\n\nThe figure matches the sum of all 14 won deals across all three reps (Okafor, Delgado, and Webb). **No update is needed** for the new contract value.\n\nHowever, I did notice **one minor inconsistency** worth flagging: the \"Next Steps\" section lists **four** pending deal IDs (D007, D013, D020, D022) but the narrative text says \"three pending deals totalling approximately $240,000.\" The CSV actually shows **five** pending deals (D007: $7,800, D013: $105,000, D018: $5,500, D020: $115,000, D022: $11,000 \u2014 totalling $244,300). So while the new contract value is accurate, the report's pending-deal count and total could use a correction if you'd like full accuracy.",
        "status_code": null
      },
